  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 220C, fan-forced. Line a large oven tray with baking paper. Wipe the mushrooms clean, then thinly slice.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3181595/photos/large/126994_1-fc66b6ae1d70e198d5fe1117deaf2453.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season mushrooms: Put the mushrooms, barbecue seasoning and 2 tsp olive oil in a bowl, season with salt and pepper and toss to coat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3181596/photos/large/126994_2-e9252760715a76aeed2790f8f4a17cee.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Assemble pita pizzas: Put 2 pita on the lined tray. Combine the tomato chutney and half the tomato paste in a bowl and spread on the pita bases. Scatter over the mushrooms and crumble over the feta.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3181598/photos/large/126994_3-21416f9b5e6e39d62fbe111a39f244a0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake pita pizzas: Bake the pizzas for 10-12 mins until golden and crisp (see Kitchen 101).",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3181599/photos/large/126994_4-ea3f98fafdc302f238fa426ecd6e9d16.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Meanwhile, combine 2 tsp olive oil and 1 tsp white wine vinegar in a large bowl and season with salt and pepper. Add the spinach and sunflower seeds and toss to combine. Cut the pizzas into wedges and serve with the salad. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3181606/photos/large/126994_5-d7fde5a5e312e6ba36eae2279dcb47c1.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: If you like your pizza bases extra crispy, spray or brush the pita with olive oil before assembling the pizza.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/3181607/photos/large/126994_6-8db4250128f840759d5643159eeae941.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
